{"availability":"available","full":"rust-ly/rustly","name":"rustly","description":"Learn Rust in your browser: the Rust Book and the Tokio tutorial as short lessons with a live editor, real compiler errors and graded exercises. Built entirely in Rust (Leptos + WebAssembly, Rust API on Vercel).","category":"Education","language":"Rust","stars":0,"forks":0,"created":"2026-10-08T15:04:03Z","updated":"2026-10-12T07:16:31Z","license":null,"branch":"main","homepage":"https://rustly-one.vercel.app","topics":["education","interactive-tutorial","learn-rust","leptos","rust","rust-book","tokio","vercel","wasm","webassembly"],"demo":"https://play.rust-lang.org/","color":"#323057","ink":"#d6caff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-12T07:59:43.782Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-12T07:59:43.782Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-12T07:59:43.782Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-12T07:59:43.782Z","stars":0,"forks":0}],"technologies":["Rust"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Learn Rust in your browser. Rustly turns The Rust Programming Language and the Tokio tutorial into short lessons with runnable examples, a real code editor and graded exercises. You don't need to install anything."],"features":["Write real Rust. Every concept ends with an exercise in a full code editor (Monaco, the editor behind VS Code). ./run shows the output. As you type, compiler errors and warnings appear as squiggles at the right spot,…","Get graded. ./submit runs hidden tests against your code and shows which ones passed. Passing a checkpoint unlocks the next concept, and passing a chapter's challenge unlocks the next chapter.","Get unstuck. Hints appear one at a time, and the solution opens after three failed submits.","Keep your place. Progress, drafts and starred snippets are saved in your browser. Export / Import moves them to another browser.","Look things up. The snippet library lists every example from the lessons you've opened, searchable, with stars."],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/rust-ly/rustly/b